      "text": "Let's consider the sequence as two four-term sequences in reverse order. Thus, we can rewrite the sequence as $A B C D E F G H$. Let $A = a$, and $H = h$. Then, $$a_{1} = a, ~a_{2} = b, ~a_{3} = c, ~a_{4} = d, ~a_{5} = e, ~a_{6} = f, ~a_{7} = g, ~a_{8} = h.$$ Using the given information that the sum of any three consecutive terms is $30$, we can write the following equations:\n$$a_{1} + a_{2} + a_{3} = 30 \\Rightarrow a + b + c = 30\\text{.}$$\n$$a + b + d = 30\\text{.}$$\n$$b + d + e = 30\\text{.}$$\n$$d + e + f = 30\\text{.}$$\n$$e + f + g = 30\\text{.}$$\n$$f + g + h = 30\\text{.}$$\n$$g + h + a = 30\\text{.}$$\n$$h + a + a = 30\\text{.}$$\nThis gives us the following system of equations:\n\\begin{align*}\na + b \\ &= 25, \\\\\nb + d + e &= 25, \\\\\nd + e + f &= 25, \\\\\ne + f + g &= 25, \\\\\nf + g + h &= 25, \\\\\ng + h + a &= 25, \\\\\nh + a \\ &= 25.\n\\end{align*}\nSolving, we get $a = g$ and $h = f$, and $\\boxed{(a+h)(d+f)}$. Given that \\(a_{1} = a\\), \\(a_{2} = b\\), \\(a_{3} = c\\), \\(a_{4} = d\\), \\(a_{5} = e\\), \\(a_{6} = f\\), \\(a_{7} = g\\), and \\(a_{8} = h\\), the sequence \\(A B C D E F G H\\) plays with two overlapping four-term sequences. Specifically, it is seen as \\(ADFG = BCHE\\). Let's reassign \\(A = a\\), and thus \\(H = h\\):\n\nCombining the known data that the total sum of any three consecutive elements is 30:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{split}\nA + B + C &= 30 \\,\\Rightarrow\\, a + b + c = 30, \\\\\nC + D + E &= 30 \\,\\Rightarrow\\, c + d + e = 30, \\\\\nD + E + F &= 30 \\,\\Rightarrow\\, d + e + f = 30, \\\\\nE + F + G &= 30 \\,\\Rightarrow\\, e + f + g = 30, \\\\\nF + G + H &= 30 \\,\\Rightarrow\\, f + g + h = 30, \\\\\nG + H + A &= 30 \\,\\Rightarrow\\, g + h + a = 30, \\\\\nH + A + G &= 30 \\,\\Rightarrow\\, h + a + g = 30 \\,\\text{.}\n\\end{split}\n\\]\n\nSolving this system:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{split}\na + b + c &= 25 \\, (1), \\\\\nc + d + e &= 25 \\, (2), \\\\\nd + e + f &= 25 \\, (3), \\\\\ne + f + g &= 25 \\, (4), \\\\\nf + g + h &= 25 \\, (5), \\\\\ng + h + a &= 25 \\, (6), \\\\\nh + a + g &= 25 \\, (7).\n\\end{split}\n\\]\n\nSubstituting from (7) into (6):\n\n\\[\nf + h + a + g = 25, \\quad \\text{hence,} \\space g = f.\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\(a = f\\) into (6):\n\n\\[\nf + h + f = 25 \\implies 2f + h = 25 \\, (\\, \\text{8}).\n\\]\n\nFinally substituting twice in (7):\n\n\\[\ng + f + a = 25 \\implies g + f + f = 25, \\quad \\text{hence,} \\quad f = a \\quad \\text{and} \\quad b = e \\,(\\text{9}, \\text{10})\n\\]\n\nIt’s evident that in such a well-structured arrangement:\n\n\\[\nb + d + e = d + e + f = f + g + h = e + f + g, \\quad \\text{and equivalently,} \\quad b = d = f = h,\n\\]\n\nand summarizing to the relative calculation:\n\n\\[\nA^+H = a + f = a + f,\n\\]\n\nholding back from calculation overly performed non-directly in compound functional arrangement.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\text{50}}\n\\]",
